  "interpretation": {
    "lwt_force_sync_path": "Pinned Scylla code marks system.paxos for commitlog sync, routes prepare/accept/learn through that path, and learn requests force_sync::yes for the committed mutation. The commitlog writer routes writer.sync through batch_cycle/sync even when periodic mode is configured; this does not establish one physical fsync per transaction or exclude coalescing. This benchmark disables tablets, so the evidence applies to the system.paxos route and does not claim behavior for tablet-backed LWT paths.",
    "official_documentation": "The pinned 2026.1 manual states that all LWT writes use synchronous commitlog mode and reach the device before LWT completion, in all commitlog_sync modes.",
    "periodic_ordinary_writes": "Pinned config documentation says periodic syncs are acknowledged immediately; this runner does not interpret ordinary periodic writes as synchronous acknowledgements."
  },
